# Keep secrets, VCS metadata, docs, caches, and local artifacts out of the Docker
# build context (nothing here is COPYed into an image; this hardens against
# accidental secret leakage and shrinks/speeds the context). Do NOT exclude apps/
# or db/ -- the images/build need them.

# Secrets / env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/
# Local TLS-interception root CA. It reaches the build ONLY as a BuildKit secret
# (read from the host path, never from the build context), so keeping it out of the
# context is free and guarantees it can never be COPYed into a layer by accident.
# Exact paths, NOT *.crt/*.cer -- a broad glob could silently hide a legitimate
# project certificate from a future build.
infra/docker/norton-webmail-root.crt
infra/docker/norton-webmail-root.cer

# VCS / CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Python caches / test artifacts
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
*.egg-info/

# Node (web app deps are installed in its own image layer)
**/node_modules/

# Docs / planning (not needed at runtime)
docs/
*.md
!apps/web/README.md

# Editor / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local model / tool caches
**/.dit/
**/nuclei-templates/
